`registry lint` runs the RFC 08 §5 lints a consumer's `build.rs` runs, without
the build — and prints the build's own wording, verbatim, because saying
exactly what the build would say is the whole value of the command.

No session: it goes straight to `zenkey_build::Config`.

```console
$ zenctl registry lint ../fixture-tests/registry
../fixture-tests/registry: registry lints pass (RFC 08 §5).

```

A directory that is not a registry fails, naming what it looked for:

```console
$ zenctl registry lint ../fixture-tests/registry/nonexistent
? 1
Error: registry dir "../fixture-tests/registry/nonexistent": No such file or directory (os error 2)

```
